From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hunter B Hough <git@hough.ink>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 16:12:09 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 124/148] refactor(witness): retire the per-bead worktree
 reaper for upstream's task-artifact lifecycle (gcp-fooz4)

The baseline move to 520e95cb brings upstream #245 (f709abe5), whose
task-artifact lifecycle owns per-bead worktree teardown on every terminal
path: the refinery records artifact_source_sha before the rebase, runs
task-artifact-cleanup after a verified close (direct) or pr-merge-reconcile
runs it after a verified merge (mr), and removal never uses --force or
trusts bead closure alone (task-artifact-cleanup.sh; help.md "Mutable bead
metadata alone is never sufficient deletion evidence").

Our witness reaper (old patches 0012-0014, 0027, 0028, 0032, 0070, 0071,
0081, 0082, 0087-0089, 0092-0095, 0100-0102, 0141) is dropped from the
stack, not reverted on top of it. It only recognised the legacy
<home>/worktrees/<bead> layout, so it cannot see upstream's
artifacts/worktrees/<bead> (measured on the tip: 0 log lines for a
canonical artifact), it was never armed live (dry-run), and its 0012 prose
("the refinery closes this bead when the PR opens") contradicts upstream's
mr lane, which blocks the bead until the merge is verified. 0010 is
superseded by upstream #320 (05031f2c) Step 2a; 0011's residual case is
re-applied separately.

This commit carries only what the drop left behind in the surviving
patches: the agent-home audit (0044/0045/0067/0080) no longer names the
reaper as the owner of per-bead children, the pre_start inventory (0030)
loses the witness row, and mol-polecat-work stops listing the reaper as a
polecat_session reader. Legacy per-bead worktrees still on disk are a
one-time operator drain.

Clears base red gcp-98gh (tests/test_no_bare_bd_commands.py flagged
docs/design/reaper-budget-starvation.md, which is gone).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
